{"text": "Melissa Fwu\n\nEXPERIENCE\nRepublican Party of July 2015 - Present\nSenior Deputy State Director Fairfax, Virginia\n\n\u2018+ Oversaw the statewide activities of 43 field staff including training and development to maximize output\ntowards RNC election efforts in a top Presidential swing state\n* Directed top performing regions which consistently exceeded voter contact goals\n* Develop and implement statewide field strategy, goals, and messaging in coordination with State Director\n* Coordinated statewide outreach and engagement efforts in the Asian, Hispanic, and faith communities\n\nRepublican Party of Texas July 2013 July 2015\nDirector of Asian American Engagement \u2018Austin, Texas\n* Developed and implemented a statewide political plan to increase Asian Pacific American (APA) Republican\nvoter turnout through identification of community partners, expanding Party's APA auxiliary to 300+ members,\nrecruiting volunteers, and organizing Republican presence at 80 community events\n* Party spokesperson to APA media sources, including television and radio interviews\n\u2018+ Efforts resulted in Texas Republicans winning 53% (US Senator Cornyn) and 51% (Texas Governor Abbott) of the\nAsian vote in Texas\n\n\u2018The European-Atlantic Group January 2011 ~ May 2011\nInternational Relations intern London, UK\n\u2018\u00a9 Organized, marketed, and executed high-profile debates featuring international political and diplomatic leaders\n\u00a9 Developed marketing and fundraising strategies as a team to produce key event sponsorships\n\nUSA Pavilion - Shanghai World Exposition May 2010 \u2014 July 2010\nStudent Ambassador \u2018Shanghai, China\n\u2018* Showcased the United States and American innovation through presentations in Mandarin Chinese and English\nto media, key stakeholders, and over 20,000 international visitors a day\n\nOther: Texas House of Representatives, Legislative Aide (2013); Rice University Centennial Celebration, Student\nRelations Specialist; Sun Max Trading Company, Exec. Assistant (2009-2011); Littleton & Associates, Legal Intern (2011)\n\nEDUCATION\nRice University May 2012\nBachelor of Arts Double Major: Political Science and Policy Studies (GPA: 3.7) Houston, Texas\n\n\u2018* Concentration in international Relations; Law and Justice\n\u2018* Rice Global Urban Lab: Semester abroad in London and Istanbul; analyzed patterns of urban development in\nOlympic host cities and determine best practices for future bids\nLanguages: Fluent in Mandarin Chinese and Proficient in Spanish\n\nACTIVITIES.\n\nBaker Institute for Public Policy - Student Forum 2009 - 2012\nEvents Chair (2011 - 2012); Communications Director (2009-2011)\n+ Lead Rice\u2019s largest political organization to promote student interest in politics and international relations\n* Directed campus-wide marketing and organizational efforts for up to 20 events a year featuring political and\ndiplomatic leaders from around the world\nRice University Honor Council 2009 - 2012\n* Elected University Representative\nBrown Residential College Committees 2009 - 2012\nSocials Coordinator; Brown Events Committee Chair; Senior Events Chair",
